7. On hearing both side the following points would arise for the determination of this Court are as follows;
POINTS 1)Whether the prosecution proves beyond all reasonable doubt that on 1.7.2018 accused got married the daughter of C.W.1 in Gayathri Temple, Yeshwanthapura, later on 22.3.2019 they got registered the marriage, later they stayed in a house bearing No.9, 2 nd floor, Maruthi Bakery, Maranna Stage,
Chkkabidarakall, Nagasandra Post, and at the time of accused received one golden dollar, and after marriage kept one necklace, one chain and one hangings in the pawn shop and received the amount and spent it, when C.W.1 questioned, accused told her to bring the amount from her parental house and give half of the house from her mother and half of the land of her father and furtherance of their common intention have subjected the victim to mental and physical cruelty to bring more dowry and abused her in filthy language and thereby committed the offence punishable under Section 498(A) of IPC?

My findings to the above points are as follows;
Point No.1 : In the Negative Point No.2 : In the Negative Point No.3 : In the Negative Point No.4 : As per final order, for the following;
REASONS 9. POINT NO.1 : The prosecution to prove the ingredients of offence punishable u/s.498A of IPC basically relies on the evidence of complainant, his son P.W.2 and husband P.W.3 who are the material witnesses who deposes about the harassment given by the accused to the victim.
